一共◆◆yīgòng◆副§§§altogether; in all; all told; overall△去车站一共要走大约一小时的时间。¦It is about an hour's walk to the station all in all.△我一共要付多少钱？¦How much shall I pay in all?△我们班一共三十人。¦There are altogether thirty people in our class.
一切◆◆yīqiè◆代§§§all; every△调动一切积极因素¦bring all positive factors into play△抓住一切机会¦seize every opportunity△他不得不想尽一切办法去争取这份工作。¦He had to move heaven and earth to get the job.▷代§§§all; everything△一切从简¦all is done in a simplified manner△一切从人民利益出发¦proceed in all cases from the interests of the people△一切缴获要归公¦turn in everything captured△一切尽归私囊¦sweep everything into one's net△一切如旧。¦Everything remains unchanged. / Everything is the same as usual.△他已失去了一切。¦He has lost his all.△这结束了我们之间的一切。¦This ends all between us forever.△好好珍惜你现在所拥有的一切吧。你现在拥有的，正是从前梦寐以求的。¦Appreciate what you have. Because what you have now is one of the things you once prayed for.
一回事◆◆yīhuíshì◆名§§§one and the same thing△你们说的不是一回事。¦You are not talking about the same thing.△这两家公司实际上是一回事。¦The two firms are actually one and the same outfit.▷名§§§one thing△说是一回事，做是另一回事。¦It's one thing to say it, quite another to do it.▷名§§§remarkable/important thing/person; something△他画得还像那么一回事。¦His paintings are really something. / He paints quite well as a matter of fact.△我只不过随便说说而已，谁知道他还把它当成一回事了。¦I said it casually but he took it very seriously.▷名§§§actual fact△根本没有那么一回事。¦That's absolutely not the case.
一天◆◆yītiān◆名§§§a day△一天又一天¦day after day▷名§§§the whole day; all day long△一天滴水未进¦have had nothing the whole day▷名§§§one day (in the past)△一天，他突然回来了。¦One day, he came home unexpectedly.
一头◆◆yītóu◆副§§§[of several things happening at the same time]△他一头说，一头朝门口走。¦While talking, he was heading for the door.▷副§§§directly; straight away△门一开，他就一头钻了进去。¦As soon as the door opened, he went in straight away.▷副§§§suddenly; unexpectedly; all of a sudden; out of one's expectation△我刚进门就一头撞上了老板。¦I bumped into the boss the moment I came in.▷副§§§headlong△一头扎进水里¦plunge headlong into the water▷名§§§one end△你那一头有没有问题？¦Are there any problems at your end?△我们从街道的一头走到另一头。¦We walked the street from end to end.△这张桌子一头高一头低。¦One end of the desk is higher than the other.▷名§§§a head△高出一头¦be taller by a head▷名§§§side; gang△站在他们一头¦be on their side▷副§§方§together△一头来¦come together
一套◆◆yītào◆名§§§one's set way△他干事有他的一套。¦He has his own set way of doing things.△她口里一套，心里又是一套。¦She says one thing and means another.▷名§§§convention; the same stuff▷量§§§a set; a flat; a suite; a suit
一定◆◆yīdìng◆形§§§fixed; specified; definite; regular△一定报酬¦definite remuneration△一定的规章制度¦specified rules and regulations△一定的生产指标¦fixed production quota△他上班时间不一定。¦He doesn't keep regular office hours.△每一种弹簧都有一定的弹性。¦Every sort of spring has definite elasticity.▷副§§§surely; certainly; necessarily△感到一定能赢¦feel quite certain/sure of winning△失败不一定是坏事。¦Failure is not necessarily a bad thing.△我猜想他一定是迷了路。¦I figured that he must have gotten lost.△下次我一定把那本书给你带来。¦I'll sure bring you that book next time, without fail.△在这儿一定要服从她。¦She should absolutely be obeyed here.▷形§§§particular; certain; given△保持一定的距离¦maintain a measured/respectful distance△引起一定的注意¦attract a measure of attention△一定量的糖¦a certain amount of sugar△在一定程度上¦to a certain extent; to some extent/degree△在一定的条件下¦under certain/given conditions△在一定意义上¦in a certain sense△我对这个课题曾有一定的了解。¦I had some previous acquaintance with the subject.▷形§§§proper; fair; due△达到一定水平¦reach a fairly high level△发挥一定的作用¦play a proper role△给予一定的重视¦give due attention to; attach due importance to△取得一定的成绩¦win fairly good achievements△在国际市场上占有一定的份额¦occupy a fairly big share in the world market△这里离火车站有一定的距离。¦It is a fair distance to the railway station from here.
