一点儿◆◆yīdiǎnr◆量§§§some△给我一点儿水喝。¦Give me some water to drink.△咱们稳妥一点儿，多带一点儿钱。¦Let's be on the safe side and take more money than we think we'll need.▷量§§§a bit; a little△一点儿不错¦be perfectly correct△一点儿不犹豫¦have no ambivalence at all; without any hesitation△一点儿不知道¦not have the faintest/slightest idea (of)△一点儿活都不干¦not do a stitch of work△一点儿也不累¦not feel the least bit tired△一点儿用处也没有¦be utterly useless△有一点儿冷¦feel a little cold△一点儿空余的地方都腾不出来。¦There is not an inch of room to spare.△你的话一点儿也不真实。¦There is not a grain of truth in your statement.△她个子矮了一点儿。¦She's a bit short/on the short side.△她没有一点儿见识。¦She hasn't got a pennyworth of sense.△我一点儿不懂你在讲些什么。¦I don't have the faintest idea of what you are talking about/driving at.
一生◆◆yīshēng◆名§§§all one's life; a span of a man's life△毁掉一生¦ruin one's/sb's life; make a mess of one's life△结束一生¦end/close one's life△虚度一生¦pass one's life idly/in idleness△影响一生¦influence one's/sb's entire life△一生坎坷¦have a bumpy life; have bad/ill/hard/tough luck all one's life△一生潦倒¦be a failure all one's life; remain poor all one's life△一生默默无闻¦remain obscure all one's life△一生飘荡¦run hither and thither all one's life△一生清贫¦be in poverty from birth to death△一生受苦¦suffer hardships throughout one's life△一生受用¦enjoy the benefit all one's life△一生辛劳¦labour uphill all one's life; a life of hardship△平淡的一生¦uneventful life△他一生从事医学研究。¦He devoted all his life to medical research.△他一生目睹了许多变化。¦He saw many changes in his lifetime.
