的◆◆de◆助§§§[used with an adjective or attribute phrase]—▲[indicating a modifying or modified relationship]⬩美好的未来¦bright future⬩铁的纪律¦iron discipline▲[indicating a possessive relationship]⬩人民的公仆¦servant of the people⬩我的父亲¦my father▲[indicating a relationship of a person and his title or capacity]⬩今天是我的东。¦I'll be the host today. / It's my treat today.⬩谁的介绍人？¦Who is the matchmaker?▲[indicating the receiver of an action]⬩别开我的玩笑。¦Don't make fun of me.⬩你净扫大家的兴。¦You are just disappointing all of us. / Don't be a wet blanket.▷助§§§[used after a noun, pronoun, verb, or an adjective to form a noun phrase without a head noun]—▲[indicating sb/sth already mentioned]⬩这铺是我的，那才是你的。¦This bunk is mine, and that is yours.⬩玫瑰花开了，有红的，有黄的。¦The roses are in bloom; some are red and some yellow.▲[indicating a certain type of person or thing]⬩男的¦male; man⬩我爱吃甜的。¦I like sweet food.▲[indicating a condition or situation]⬩大热天的，你还来看我。¦It's very kind of you to come and see me on such a hot day.⬩无缘无故的，他瞪你干什么？¦Why on earth did he glare at you? There's got to be a reason.▲[indicating a subject that has nothing to do with what is going on]⬩我能行，你忙你的去吧。¦I can manage. You just get on with your work.▲[indicating diversity]⬩推的推，拉的拉。¦Some are pushing and some are pulling.⬩说的说，笑的笑。¦Some are talking and some laughing.⬩大的大，小的小。¦Some (of them) are big and some small.▷助§§§[used after the predicative verb to emphasize the doer, the time, the place, etc]▷助§§§[used at the end of a declarative sentence to give a positive tone to the statement]▷助§§§[used after two things of the same kind to imply 'and so on' or 'and the like']▷助§§§[used between two numerals]—▲[indicating multiplication]⬩这间教室是三米的六米，合十八平方米。¦This classroom is three metres by six, with a total floor space of eighteen square metres.▲[indicating addition]⬩四块的五块，一共九块。¦Four yuan plus five yuan is nine yuan .
